'''''Rhynchoconger bicoloratus'''''<ref>{{Cite web |title=CAS - Eschmeyer's Catalog of Fishes |url=https://researcharchive.calacademy.org/research/ichthyology/catalog/fishcatmain.asp |access-date=2023-11-29 |website=researcharchive.calacademy.org}}</ref> is a species of deep-water [[Congridae|conger eel]] native to the [[Indian Ocean]]. It was described through specimens captured in Kalamukku fishing harbor, off [[Kochi]], [[Arabian Sea]], from a depth beyond 200 m.<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Kodeeswaran |first1=Paramasivam |last2=Mohapatra |first2=Anil |last3=Kumar |first3=Thipramalai Thangappan Pillai Ajith |last4=Lal |first4=Kuldeep Kumar |date=May 2023 |title=A new deep-water conger eel of the genus Rhynchoconger ( Anguilliformes: Congridae ) from the south-west coast of India, Arabian Sea |url=https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/jfb.15367 |journal=Journal of Fish Biology |language=en |volume=102 |issue=5 |pages=1245–1252 |doi=10.1111/jfb.15367 |pmid=36880271 |bibcode=2023JFBio.102.1245K |issn=0022-1112|url-access=subscription }}</ref>

